<%# (a) The exploded guitar, as the page's background.

    Fixed behind everything, with the page's own scroll as its progress: fully
    assembled at the top, fully apart at the bottom. There is no panel, no
    heading and no control, because this is the ground the page stands on rather
    than a piece of furniture in it.

    pointer-events-none so it never eats a click meant for the page, and -z-10 so
    it paints above the root background but below every element of content.

    The model goes through the asset pipeline so it is fingerprinted. In public/
    it would be served at a fixed URL, so replacing it would be invisible and the
    page would keep rendering the previous instrument. %>
<div class="pointer-events-none fixed inset-0 -z-10"
     data-controller="exploded-guitar"
     data-exploded-guitar-url-value="<%= asset_path("exploded_guitar.glb") %>">
  <canvas data-exploded-guitar-target="canvas"
          class="block h-full w-full"
          role="img"
          aria-label="An electric guitar in three dimensions, behind the page. Scrolling takes it apart."></canvas>
</div>
